# Hilos Framework

Read `agents.md` before starting work in this repository. Use it as the rule
index and follow the relevant `docs/agents/*` files before editing.

Rules are layered:

- `agents.md` contains repository-wide hard stops and navigation.
- `docs/agents/*` contains the canonical task-specific rules.
- `skills/hilos-*` holds wrappers for the CLI agents — Codex and Cursor alike;
  do not treat them as a separate source of truth.

When changing DB entity shape, RT item shape, signal DTO payloads, declarative
routing, or page/worker routes, stop and ask the user for explicit confirmation
as described in `agents.md`.

Never run `git push`. Publishing is the owner's, and a hook enforces it.

Commit only the leaf you were given, and only on its own `HIL-<n>` branch —
that is how the headless line records work, and a turn that refuses to commit
loses it. Outside a leaf of your own, do not commit at all.
